03A9:                   * Find opcode match
03A9:                   * Entry: Y=Table ptr to look in for match
03A9:                   *        X=Ptr to part of source we are currently checking
03A9:                   *        B=# opcodes in current table
03A9:                   * Exit: Carry set if no matching mnemonic found (and X points to start of bad mnemonic)
03A9:                   *       Carry clear, Y is ptr to opcode & flag bytes, X=ptr to byte after mnemonic if match IS found
03A9:                   * LCB - Optimized to use DP instead of stack for X (since only needed for non-match),
03A9:                   *   and not preserving B at all (always reset by calling routines)
03A9:                   * If this works, may also be able to stx <TmpNum
03A9: 9F67              L0344    stx   <TmpNum        Preserve source code ptr & # opcodes in table
03AB: A6A0              L0346    lda   ,y+            Get byte from table
03AD: 2B13                       bmi   L035E          If high bit set, skip ahead
03AF: A880                       eora  ,x+            Do characters match?
03B1: 84DF                       anda  #$DF           Ignore case mismatch
03B3: 27F6                       beq   L0346          If matches, keep doing until last character
03B5: A6A0              L0350    lda   ,y+            Doesn't match, search for end of current entry
03B7: 2AFC                       bpl   L0350
03B9: 3122              L0354    leay  2,y            Skip opcode & flag bytes too
03BB: 9E67                       ldx   <TmpNum        Reset source code ptr to start of instruction
03BD: 5A                         decb                 Dec # opcodes counter
03BE: 26EB                       bne   L0346          Check until all are done
