03CA:                   
03CA:                   * Opcode & Pseudo Opcode Table
03CA:                   * Mnemonic words are high bit terminated
03CA:                   * First numeric byte is the base opcode (before addressing modes considered)
03CA:                   * 2nd is flags:
03CA:                   * Least significiant 4 bits = index into handler table
03CA:                   * 0= LBRA & LBSR (non comparitive long branches/no pre-byte)
03CA:                   * 1= Immediate (no register options) ex. ORCC
03CA:                   * 2= 16 bit register commands
03CA:                   * 3= 8 bit register commands
03CA:                   * 4= CLR, etc. Inherent (A,B,D,E,F,W all supported)
03CA:                   * 5= 'Fixed' (register not negotiable) inherent commands
03CA:                   * 6= LEAx - Indexed only
03CA:                   * 7= Register to register (TFR,EXG) (now patched for dual size 0 register)
03CA:                   * 8= Stack push/pull (except for W - it's done as type 5)
03CA:                   * 9= 16 bit Relative comparative branches setup flag
03CA:                   * A= 8 bit Relative comparative branches
03CA:                   * B= Pseudo op
03CA:                   * C= Pseudo op (label not allowed)
03CA:                   * D= Pseudo op conditionals (IFxx)
03CA:                   * E= Pseudo op (ELSE & ENDC)
03CA:                   * F= 6309 bit ops (OIM,BAND,etc) (was UNUSED)
03CA:                   * Most significiant 4 bits
03CA:                   * %00010000 : $10 prefix byte always needed
03CA:                   * %00100000 : $11 prefix byte always needed
03CA:                   * %01000000 : Immediate mode illegal
03CA:                   * %10000000 : Default to extended mode - not used??? RVH
03CA:                   
