1AFD:                   * Stack Blast clear routine for speed (both 6809/6309)
1AFD:                   * Entry: B=Value to clear with (single byte). NOTE: If you enter at StkBlCl2, you can 
1AFD:                   *          have D=double byte value to clear with (useful for hardware text screens, like in
1AFD:                   *          Level II grfdrv)
1AFD:                   *        X=Size (in bytes) to clear
1AFD:                   *        U=Start address to clear from
1AFD:                   * NOTE: No incoming regs preserved!
1AFD:                   * NOTE: If you have a 2 byte value (hware text), put that in D, and call via StkBlCl2
1AFD:                   * NOTE 2: If you know you are doing an even 4 byte sized clear, you can preload X with the value(s)
1AFD:                   *    to clear with, A:B as the # of 4 byte chunks, and U as the ptr to then end of the clear,
1AFD:                   *    and jump straight to either NormClr. You do have to add 3 bytes to the stack first
1AFD: 1F98              StkBlClr tfr   b,a            D=double copy of value to clear memory with
1AFF: 1E10              StkBlCl2 exg   x,d            D=Size to clear (in bytes), X=2 byte value to clear with
1B01:                          IFNE  H6309
1B01:                            addr  d,u            Point to end of clear area for stack blast
1B01:                          ELSE
1B01: 33CB                       leau  d,u            Point to end of clear area for stack blast
1B03:                          ENDC
1B03: 3414                       pshs  b,x            Save 16 bit value to clear with, & LSB of size (to check for leftover bytes)
1B05: 44                         lsra                 Divide size by 4 (since we are doing 4 bytes at a time)
1B06: 56                         rorb
1B07: 44                         lsra
1B08: 56                         rorb
1B09: 3406                       pshs  d              Save mini-stackblast counters
1B0B: EC62                       ldd   2,s            Get A=LSB of # of bytes to clear, B=byte to clear with
1B0D: 8403                       anda  #%00000011     Non-even multiple of 4?
1B0F: 270A                       beq   NoOdd          Even, skip single byte cleanup copy
1B11: 44                OverLp   lsra                 Odd # of bytes?
1B12: 2405                       bcc    Do2           No, skip to 2 byte copy (can only be 2 at this point)
1B14: E7C2                       stb    ,-u           Yes, save 1 byte (could be 1 or 3)
1B16: 44                Chk2Byte lsra                 Double byte as well?
1B17: 2402                       bcc    NoOdd         No, do 4 byte chunks if needed
1B19: AFC3              Do2      stx   ,--u           Save double byte value
1B1B: ECE1              NoOdd    ldd   ,s++           Get Mini-stack blast ctrs back
1B1D: 270A                       beq   ExitClrB       No 4 byte blocks, done
1B1F: 3184              NormClr  leay  ,x             Dupe 16 bit clear value to Y
1B21: 3630              ClrLp    pshu  x,y            Clear 4 bytes
1B23: 5A                         decb                 Dec "leftover" (<256) 4 byte block counter
1B24: 26FB                       bne   ClrLp          Keep doing till that chunk is done
1B26: 4A                         deca                 Dec 1Kbyte counter
1B27: 2AF8                       bpl   ClrLp          Still going (B has been set to 0, so inner loop is 256 now)
1B29: 3594              ExitClrB puls  b,x,pc         Eat temp regs & return
